     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 850 mg to 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** If so, please tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm that explicitly. I can then enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose, though I'd recommend against it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
